rap_or(Bare)`, then `resolve_id` at 318) | The one selector resolver. | Yes (via #1) | Is the resolver |\n  | 3 | `crates/callisto-graph/src/aggregate.rs:317` (`PackageId::parse(&entry.name)`, then `resolve_target_package` at 193-203, which calls `resolve_id` at 198) | Changeset frontmatter keys, in `callisto version` | Yes | Yes (`resolve_id`) |\n  | 4 | `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/status.rs:40` (then `resolve_target_package` at 43) and `status.rs:203` (well-formedness diagnostics, then 204) | Changeset frontmatter keys, in `callisto status` | Yes | Yes (`resolve_id`) |\n  | 5 | `crates/callisto-model/src/format/changeset/frontmatter.rs:44-62` (`split_name_and_rest`: `rsplit_once(':')` for bare names, quote-scan for quoted names). Does not call `PackageId::parse`. | Changeset line tokenizer | A bare `cargo:foo: patch` splits at the last `:`, so the name becomes `cargo:foo`. A quoted `\"cargo:foo\": patch` also keeps it. `needs_quoting` quotes any name containing `:` (about lines 105-112). Colon is not rejected here, only at #3 and #4. | No, tokenizer only |\n  | 6 | `crates/callisto-graph/src/lib.rs:363` (`identity.resolve(key)`) and `lib.rs:367` (`PackageId::parse(key).is_ok_and(ecosystem().is_some())`), inside `assign_promoted_pre_keys`. `pre_json_key` at lib.rs:293 uses `display_name()`. | `pre.json` `initialVersions` keys | Yes | Yes (`resolve`) |\n  | 7 | `crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/add.rs:26-35`: `pkg_str.rsplit_once(':')` splits off the severity, then `ws.identity.resolve(name)`. The entry is written as `resolved.display_name()` (slash). | `callisto add --package NAME:SEVERITY`. Flag at `cli.rs:141`, error E270 at `cli/error.rs:326`. | Yes. `cargo:foo:patch` splits to name `cargo:foo`. | Yes (`resolve`) |\n  | 8 | `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/matrix.rs:~31-34`, `resolve_selected_package` at 112-123, `identity.resolve(raw)` at 116. Flag at `cli.rs:162-165`. | `callisto matrix --package` | Yes | Yes (`resolve`) |\n  | 9 | `crates/callisto-graph/src/config/groups.rs:186` (`index.resolve(name)`). A platform-manifest name lookup precedes it at line 177 (`index.platform.get(name)`). | `callisto.toml` `[[fixed-group]]` and `[[linked-group]]` `members` | Yes | Yes (`resolve`) |\n  | 10 | `crates/callisto-graph/src/config/resolve.rs:161-170` (`parse_qualified_package`, `PackageId::parse` then requires `ecosystem().is_some()`), called at 174 and 182. Matched later through `identifies` at `commands/matrix.rs:66,74` and `commands/release/derive.rs:659,664,696,848`. | `callisto.toml` `[release] product-package` and `[[release.artifact]] package` | Yes | Yes (`identifies`, which calls `resolve_id`) |\n  | 11 | `crates/callisto-graph/src/config/resolve.rs:594` (`PackageId::parse(&raw_pkg.pattern)`). Matching is `rule_applies` at 311 and `resolve_package_config` at 334-360, comparing name and ecosystem directly. | `callisto.toml` `[[package]] match` | Yes | No. The identity index is bypassed, as in the V1-SYSTEM-HARDENING \"match through the identity index\" slice. |\n  | 12 | `crates/callisto-graph/src/config/pattern.rs:26-33` (`PackagePattern::parse`: `[':', '/']` loop, then `Glob::new(rest)`). Called at `resolve.rs:629`. | `callisto.toml` `[[package-set]] match` (a glob language) | Yes. `:` is tried first, with an explicit comment keeping it. | No (`matches_in_ecosystems`, used from walk.rs) |\n  | 13 | `crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/release.rs:189-202` (`parse_release_selection`, `PackageId::parse`, then `ReleasePackageId::new`). Called via `parse_selections` at 180, from release.rs:56 and 436. Error text at line 199 recommends `` `cargo/pkg` or `cargo:pkg` ``. | `callisto release --package` (`cli.rs:268`) and `callisto release plan --package` (`cli.rs:363`) | Yes. Colon is normalised to a `ReleasePackageId` (slash). | No. `release_decision.rs:92-109` (`workspace_package`) compares `ReleasePackageId` values directly. |\n  | 14 | `crates/callisto-model/src/release/package_id.rs:~62` (`ReleasePackageId::parse