{"parentUuid":null,"logicalParentUuid":"7d258049-920c-4e13-a9c2-caf5c15046c4","isSidechain":false,"type":"system","subtype":"compact_boundary","content":"Conversation compacted","isMeta":false,"timestamp":"2026-10-21T05:37:09.304Z","uuid":"9cbc69d9-346c-4e57-84a6-25749fd23596","level":"info","compactMetadata":{"trigger":"auto","preTokens":212357,"durationMs":46373,"preCompactDiscoveredTools":["ExitWorktree","Monitor","SendMessage","WebFetch","WebSearch"],"preservedSegment":{"headUuid":"774a4d77-8f0e-4a44-a6c3-cce678b9f942","anchorUuid":"deccee77-bd9e-434b-99b7-5c2675a02388","tailUuid":"7d258049-920c-4e13-a9c2-caf5c15046c4"},"preservedMessages":{"anchorUuid":"deccee77-bd9e-434b-99b7-5c2675a02388","uuids":["774a4d77-8f0e-4a44-a6c3-cce678b9f942","6967b5f6-e877-4312-9df7-0186e811a205","c7fcb461-28bd-44b9-9847-c433b433c6ac","7d258049-920c-4e13-a9c2-caf5c15046c4"],"allUuids":["774a4d77-8f0e-4a44-a6c3-cce678b9f942","6967b5f6-e877-4312-9df7-0186e811a205","d95e5a59-230c-4dc4-a5df-c659125ce185","c7fcb461-28bd-44b9-9847-c433b433c6ac","7d258049-920c-4e13-a9c2-caf5c15046c4"]},"postTokens":20539,"cumulativeDroppedTokens":4571787},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/t06-colon","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.292","gitBranch":"fix/reject-colon-references","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"9cbc69d9-346c-4e57-84a6-25749fd23596","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0ab5f828-ab05-41d0-8600-71b07d84fa8e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Callisto (Rust release manager for Cargo/npm/PyPI monorepos) is being driven to v1 with PRs the user merges. The earlier stretch produced 16 fix PRs, listed in the earlier summary. This stretch's user requests, in order:\n   - \"Should any or all of them be stacked in some way?\" Answered: only #266 and #267 conflicted; stack #267 on #266, leave the rest.\n   - \"Why are my commits no longer signed????\" Cause: I passed `-c commit.gpgsign=false` on 17 commit commands.\n   - \"We need to fix all of the commits that were not signed. We can't merges without signed commits\". All 17 commits were re-signed and force-pushed.\n   - \"Move all PRs from draft mode\". Done.\n   - \"All merged, what's next?\" Followed by a mid-turn \"This has conflicts: https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/pull/267\". Fixed by rebase.\n   - \"Keep going\". Worktree and branch cleanup, then T06 PR 2 (reject the colon form of package references, E316).\n   - Mid-turn: \"Don't create the PRs as draft\". Standing instruction: open all PRs ready for review.\n   - User comment on signing: \"My other sessions did it fine, you did it here\". Standing lesson: always commit with plain `git commit` (signing on). Never use `-c commit.gpgsign=false` on real repos.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Commit signing: global `commit.gpgsign=true`, key `0E16D2800539671F`; verify with `git log '--format=%G?'` (`G` = good) and GitHub's `commit.verification.verified`. `gpgsign=false` is only for scratch or fixture repos.\n   - Re-signing procedure: cherry-pick `-S` each commit onto the new signed parent in a scratch worktree, compare trees, `git push --no-verify --force-with-lease=refs/heads/<br>:<old> origin <new>:refs/heads/<br>`, then sync local branches and worktrees.\n   - ADR 12 / T06 canonical references. The colon form is rejected everywhere; the slash form `eco/name` is canonical; `display_name()` already emits slash. Changesets and `pre.json` keep native or bare names, with a hard error for colon. E316 is the colon rejection; E317 (bare reference in config rejected with a fix-it) is not yet built.\n   - Error plumbing: `GraphError::Config(#[from] ConfigError)` is transparent; `CliError::Graph(#[from] GraphError)`. The registry test `error_registry_architecture.rs` requires every Diagnostic variant to carry a code. `docs/errors.md` holds the E-code table and a total count.\n   - Other facts: native GitHub stacks (`gh stack`); `just ci` includes a 90% coverage gate; AGENTS.md rules (no spec IDs in code, succinct docs, one changeset per user-visible topic, never hard-wrap Markdown, no claude.ai links in PRs/commits).\n   - zsh quirks: quote `%G?`; use `${var}` before `:`; use `${=var}` for word splitting; no `declare -A` in bash 3.2.\n   - Process notes: background-task \"exit code 0\" can be the wrapper's; always read the `exit=` line in `ci_*.log`. Auto-mode classifier can reject a Bash call when a hook rewrites it; retry once.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections (T06 PR 2, branch `fix/reject-colon-references`, commit 457833ebf, PR #270):\n   - `crates/callisto-model/src/identity.rs`: added `PackageId::colon_form_canonical`:\n     ```rust\n     pub fn colon_form_canonical(s: &str) -> Option<String> {\n         let (prefix, remainder) = s.split_once(':')?;\n         (Ecosystem::from_prefix(prefix).is_some() && !remainder.is_empty()).then(|| format!(\"{prefix}/{remainder}\"))\n     }\n     ```\n   - `crates/callisto-graph/src/error.rs`: new variant `ColonReference { context, given, canonical }` (`#[error(\"{context}: `{given}` uses the colon form, which is not accepted\")]`, `code(E316)`, help \"Write the ecosystem and name with a slash: `{canonical}`.\"); `impl ConfigError { pub fn reject_colon_form(raw: &str, context: &str) -> Result<(), Self> }` placed before the last `#[cfg(test)]`.\n   - `crates/callisto-graph/src/identity.rs`: `resolve()` calls `ConfigError::reject_colon_form(selector, \"package selector\")?`; imports `ConfigError`; dependency-ambiguity diagnostic now formats `\"{}/{n}\"`; doc comment updated; tests converted.\n   - `crates/callisto-graph/src/config/resolve.rs`: `reject_colon_form` in `parse_qualified_package` (context = key), `[[package]] match`, `[[package-set]] match`.\n   - `crates/callisto-graph/src/config/pattern.rs`: `PackagePattern::parse` is slash-only; tests and doc comment converted.\n   - `crates/callisto-graph/src/config/groups.rs`: only `GraphError::UnknownPackage` maps to `MissingGroupMember`; other errors (E103, E316) propagate (previously a catch-all `Err(_)` hid them).\n   - `crates/callisto-graph/src/aggregate.rs`: `load_changesets_permissive` rejects colon entry names with context `changeset `<path>``; imports `ConfigError`.\n   - `crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/release.rs`: `parse_release_selection` first calls `callisto_graph::ConfigError::reject_colon_form(raw, \"--package\").map_err(callisto_graph::GraphError::Config)?`; doc comment and error detail text updated; the unit test now asserts rejection naming `cargo/pkg`.\n   - Tests converted or added: graph `aggregate/tests.rs`, `walk/tests.rs`, `tests/config_resolve_tests.rs` (new `a_group_member_in_the_colon_form_is_rejected_with_the_slash_form_named`, asserts E316 and the help text), `tests/pre_baseline_conflict_tests.rs` (rewrote into `a_colon_key_is_rejected_with_the_slash_form_named` and `a_bare_key_and_its_canonical_key_conflict_unless_they_agree`), `tests/ecosystem_bugs_test.rs`, `tests/package_set_ecosystem_test.rs`. CLI `status_version_selector_tests.rs` (new tests for a colon changeset entry on `status`/`version`, and `add --package cargo:foo:minor`; colon selectors removed), `pre_mode_tests.rs`, `release_command_e2e_tests.rs`.\n   - Docs: `docs/errors.md` (E316 row after E315; \"241 numeric E#### codes\"), `docs/specs/workspace.json` (WS-ID-12 added; colon removed from the descriptions, signatures and criteria), `docs/specs/cli.json`, `docs/architecture/identity.md`, `.changeset/reject-colon-references.md` (`callisto-cli: minor`).\n   - Scratch files in `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c/scratchpad/`: `resign.sh`, `resign_tips.txt`, `ci_stack.sh <worktree> <log>`, `ci_t06p2.log`, `pr_colon.md`, `pr_files.txt`.\n   - Local plan files in `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/plans/` (git-excluded): `NEXT-WORK.md` (still lists the 16 PRs as open and needs updating), `V1-REVIEW-2026-10-20.md`, `D01-DECISIONS.md`.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Unsigned commits (my fault, 17 commit commands with `-c commit.gpgsign=false`): re-signed and force-pushed; GitHub verified all 17; do not repeat.\n   - Pushing with `$new:refs/...` in zsh failed (\"src refspec ... does not match any\"); used `${new}:refs/heads/${br}`.\n   - `declare -A` unsupported in bash 3.2; script moved to zsh with `typeset -A` and `${=commits}`.\n   - `git log --format=%G?` glob error in zsh; quoted it.\n   - #267 conflict (the shared test file with #266): rebased, kept both tests, fixed the markers with Python, tests passed (20), pushed with a lease.\n   - Python substitution scripts aborted on count mismatches (`cargo:internal-*` appeared more than once, `a `pypi:foo` rule` appeared twice); re-ran with replace-all.\n   - New test showed group resolution reported \"was not found in the workspace\" for a colon member; fixed in `groups.rs` as above.\n   - `Workspace` lacks `Debug`, so `expect_err` failed to compile; replaced with `let Err(error) = ... else { panic!(...) }`.\n   - `just ci` lint failure (`single_element_loop` in two CLI test files); unrolled the loops, reran, passed.\n   - Misleading \"exit code 0\" task notification for the first CI run (actual `exit=101`); caught by reading the log.\n   - One Bash call was rejected by the classifier because a hook changed its input; the retry worked.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Stacking analysis showed only #266/#267 conflicted; #267 was resolved by rebase and has merged.\n   - Signing fix completed across all PR branches; PRs then merged.\n   - T06 PR 2 implemented, `just ci` green (92.78% coverage), PR #270 open (non-draft, UNSTABLE while CI runs).\n   - Known gaps not done: `resolve_human` (dead code) still parses colon (planned deletion in T06 PR 1); E317 not implemented; `PackageId::parse` still reads colon internally by design.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"Should any or all of them be stacked in some way?\"\n   - \"Why are my commits no longer signed????\"\n   - \"My other sessions did it fine, you did it here\"\n   - \"We need to fix all of the commits that were not signed. We can't merges without signed commits\"\n   - \"Move all PRs from draft mode\"\n   - \"All merged, what's next?\"\n   - \"This has conflicts: https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/pull/267\"\n   - \"Keep going\"\n   - \"Don't create the PRs as draft\"\n   (Subagent hand-backs and task notifications carried no user authority. The earlier-session user messages are in the previous summary: \"What are the highest priority things for v1?\", the D01 decisions, \"Let's validate the agent findings please\", \"Let's make PRs for our fixes and stack them until done\", and others.)\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Watch CI on PR #270 (the T06 PR 2 colon rejection) and report when green; the user merges.\n   - Update local `.claude/plans/NEXT-WORK.md`: drop the shipped items and add #270. The 16-PR table is stale; all but #270 are merged. (I proposed this earlier and it is not yet done.)\n   - Remaining decision-free v1 work: T06 PRs 3 to 5 (canonical-required config E317, canonical CLI arguments, canonical emission and the report schemaVersion decision), a MSRV CI job plus scheduled `cargo deny` and Cargo dependabot, semver-checks in CI, fuzz targets for manifest editors, edition 2024/resolver 3, panic hygiene, T12a harness work.\n   - Owner decisions still open (from `V1-REVIEW-2026-10-20.md` section D): OIDC trusted publishing, which crates reach 1.0, pre mode on the managed route, snapshot publishing and dist-tag policy, schemaVersion bump with T06, E176/E157 detail, inferred-only managed releases, provenance check, Python dev groups, floating `@v1`, platform scope.\n   - Standing rules: commits must be signed (plain `git commit`); PRs must not be drafts.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Immediately before this summary request I had just created and verified PR #270 for T06 PR 2. The last command output was: `draft=false base=main UNSTABLE`, `#267 MERGED`, and commit 457833ebf `verified=true`. I had not yet written a closing message to the user for this PR. The T06 colon-rejection implementation, tests, docs and changeset were complete, `just ci` passed (`exit=0`), and the commit was signed and pushed on branch `fix/reject-colon-references` in worktree `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/t06-colon`.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Report PR #270 to the user (non-draft, signed and verified, local `just ci` green, hosted CI pending) and check hosted CI. User's latest standing instructions: \"Keep going\" and \"Don't create the PRs as draft\". Then update `.claude/plans/NEXT-WORK.md` for the merged PRs and #270. Ask before starting T06 PR 3 (canonical-required config, E317), since it is the next slice but changes behavior (bare config references would be rejected). Do not start it without confirming.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/gabe/.claude/projects/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"deccee77-bd9e-434b-99b7-5c2675a02388","timestamp":"2026-10-21T05:37:09.302Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":85,"turnIndex":181},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/t06-colon","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.292","gitBranch":"fix/reject-colon-references","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
