3f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/plans","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"stack/docs-v1","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"c4187a56-ce94-44df-93c6-e00571bd84a9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"127e6260-98ab-4e06-9352-e8746af46641","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Uf4n7mRhUDHWUMPZG3hgD4","type":"tool_result","content":"# v1 verification and adversarial review (2026-10-20)\n\nLocal only, never PR it. Baseline: main `d1f0de357` (v0.11.0). Twelve read-only research passes, each against the real binary, scratch repos and source. I re-ran these myself and they reproduce: E007 (Maturin), bare-tag adoption (S3), stale prerelease range after a pre cycle (S1), pre mode failing on the managed route (E165), the `Bearer` token leak in E163, `id-token` banned outside `build-artifact` by the policy script, and `edition = \"2021\"`. Everything else below is an agent finding with its evidence tag, not independently re-run. Scratch evidence is under `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c/scratchpad/r2/` (`t06`, `owner`, `graph`, `redact`, `small`, `verify`, `onedot`, `arch`, `specs`, `rust`, `pub`, `plan`).\n\nCorrection to D01-DECISIONS.md: the E101 spec and code do not disagree. Two default templates cannot collide (E100 forbids duplicate ids), so `has_default && ids.len() > 1` is equivalent to WS-ID-08. The real gap is that two packages with the same explicit `tag-template` pass silently. The stale `default_for` doc comment (`tag.rs:71`) is confirmed.\n\n## Can we tackle all of v1?\n\nD01 no longer blocks T06 or T08. The plan was incomplete, though: the review found defects that no task covers, and the work is about 25 PRs, not one push. Cargo builds and `just ci` stay serial.\n\n## A. Defects in no plan task (existing contracts, start now)\n\n| # | Defect | Evidence | Severity |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| A1 | A package renamed or lookalike adopts another package's tag; after a rename the real Cargo `foo` is treated as already tagged and never published (S3b) | Reproduced twice | High: silent skipped publish |\n| A2 | The local and generated-simple routes release HEAD, not the commit that introduced the version. A crashed run at A then `release` at B tags B with code that never shipped. Concurrent runs make a rerun fail permanently with E167 whose help is wrong. The generated simple workflow has no `concurrency:` group | Reproduced (agent) | High |\n| A3 | Pre-release mode fails on the managed route (E165 no changeset consumed), and `version` keeps bumping beta.0, beta.1, beta.2 with no changeset | Reproduced (me and agent) | High: prereleases only work locally |\n| A4 | After a pre cycle, a dependent keeps `^2.0.0-next.0`; a later major leaves it excluding the new dependency; `version` exits 0 with only a warning. Also: an unrepresentable peer or compound range is a warning, and a Cargo compound range half-applies the tree then fails at lockfile refresh (E208, then E121 on rerun) | Reproduced (me for npm) | High: wrong published ranges |\n| A5 | A foreign or already-published untagged version is adopted and tagged (\"already published; skipping\", then tags HEAD). No check that the registry package belongs to this repo | Reproduced (agent, `itoa`) | Medium-High |\n| A6 | Snapshot: rewrites every package with no changeset, leaves dependents on stable ranges, and `release --dry-run` after it plans a real git tag and npm publish. All prereleases and snapshots publish to dist-tag `next` | Reproduced (agent) | Medium-High, one-way door (dist-tag) |\n| A7 | Secret redaction is exact env value plus URL userinfo. A token not in a known variable (`Bearer npm_...`) prints in cleartext in live stderr, E163 text and the JSON error. Indeterminate observations (E176) show no tool text at all; E157 has no cause | Reproduced (me and agent) | Medium (security hygiene) |\n| A8 | Dual Cargo+npm `--package` selection plans the shared tag after one publish (E1); product announcement does not wait for a plugin's publish (E2); a dependent waits on every publish of its dependency (over-serialization) | Reproduced | Medium |\n| A9 | Poetry caret or tilde on a co-released dependency is not rewritten (only `==`, `~=`, `>=`, `>=,<` are); `>=0.1.0,<0.2` is rewritten to `>=0.2.0, <1`, widening past the 0.x boundary; Python dev tables are silently skipped | Reproduced (agent) | Medium |\n| A10 | Real-registry tests skip silently and report as passes; the PyPI test bypasses production binding and its index is HTML (production needs JSON); the file is Linux-only | Source and reproduced | Medium: false assurance |\n| A11 | A failed release cannot be inspected read-only; a publish that landed then reports E163 \"retry\" | Reproduced | Medium-Low |\n| A12 | `version` with an unknown changeset entry leaves the file, so its resolvable entries apply again on the next run | Reproduced (agent) | Medium-Low |\n| A13 | No monotonic guard: tag `libx@1.5.0` with manifest 0.1.1 plans 0.1.2 | Reproduced | Low (guard judged unsound; ownership fix covers it) |\n\n## B. Plan tasks, verified and re-sliced\n\n## C. 1.0 hygiene (Rust and publishing practice)\n\n- Metadata: crates inherit only `edition` and `repository`; add `rust-version`, `keywords`, `categories`, `homepage`; per-crate `documentation`; `exclude` tests and `proptest-regressions`; real READMEs with absolute links. (S)\n- MSRV is declared (1.96) but never tested; add a CI job. Edition 2021 -> 2024 and resolver 3; state an N-2 MSRV policy. Current stable is 1.99.1 (web). (S-M)\n- Panic hygiene: `unwrap_used` and `expect_used` are explicitly `allow` (about 66 unwrap, 48 expect in non-test code, estimates). `#![allow(clippy::result_large_err)]` crate-wide. (M)\n- `cargo-semver-checks` runs nowhere in CI; about 1,050 `pub` items across four library crates; `#[non_exhaustive]` uneven (manifests 0). #249 added a field to the public `RegistryConfig` without a Breaking note. (S-M)\n- Supply chain: weekly `cargo deny` advisories, Cargo dependabot, remove `AGPL-3.0-only` allowance, dead deps (`path-slash`, `fs2`), consider `cargo auditable`. (S)\n- Fuzz targets: 2 (`parse_changeset`, `parse_package_id`); none for the manifest editors. (M)\n- Publishing practice (2026 norm): crates.io, npm and PyPI trusted publishing (OIDC) and PyPI attestations; GitHub immutable releases; checksum sidecars (cargo-dist default). Callisto still needs `CARGO_REGISTRY_TOKEN`, `NPM_TOKEN` and `PYPI_TOKEN`; `.github/tests/verify-release-workflow-policy.sh` bans `id-token` outside `build-artifact` (my check) and its self-test requires `execute` to hold exactly the one secret. AGENTS.md does not ban OIDC in `execute`. First publish must be manual on crates.io and npm; the bootstrap is undocumented. Immutable releases make the documented `gh release delete-asset` recovery impossible after publish.\n- Docs stale at 1.0: README and SECURITY.md say pre-v1; `how-callisto-works.md` lines 81-83 still list three limits that shipped; `releasing.md` retry limit and napi roster; ADRs 9 and 10 are still Proposed although shipped; `publishing.md` says to map `PYPI_TOKEN` to `TWINE_PASSWORD` though the action does; `init`/`--help` banner says \"Rust workspaces\"; E227 help still advertises `cargo:pkg`.\n- Spec drift: about 13 of about 95 sampled criteria are false or partly true (14%). Examples: dirty worktree is E267 and shallow clone is E266, not E051; VER-CS-07 cites E049, which does not exist; VER-AGG-03 says `version` warns on an unknown package and it does not; MX-OUT-03 says matrix JSON has no `command` key and it does; VER-APPLY-14 says \"existing lockfile\" but `version` creates one; decision `edgeKind` spells `\"Runtime\"` vs `\"peer\"`. Error codes: 259 in docs and code match exactly; 154 are in no spec; 4 documented codes are never constructed (E050, E161, E248, E253); some duplicate meanings. Coverage: `compose-pr-body`, `release inspect`, `release build-python`, `previous-tag-templates`, the tag-template grammar and most action inputs have no criterion.\n- Contracts to pin before 1.0 (one-way doors): tag format (promotion flips the namespace), report key forms, config keys (`deny_unknown_fields`, no schema version), decision file path and schema, dist-tag policy, error-code stability, action inputs, which library API is public, `schemaVersion` meaning.\n- Platform coverage: release binaries are aarch64-apple, x86_64-linux gnu and musl only; no Intel mac, aarch64-linux or Windows.\n- Version strategy: a fixed group of all five crates means any library break forces a CLI major; `callisto-cli:major` plans all five from 0.11.0 to 1.0.0. #248 is the 0.12.0 release (8 changesets, no status checks).\n\n## D. Decisions needed from the owner\n\n1. OIDC: allow `id-token: write` on `execute` (secrets optional) and change the policy script, or keep long-lived tokens for 1.0 and document it.\n2. Library crates at 1.0: only `callisto-cli` at 1.0 with the libraries documented unstable and split out of the fixed group (agents' lean), or all four.\n3. Pre-release mode on the managed route (A3): support it (needs a verification rule that accepts retained changesets and no empty bump churn) or document it as local-only.\n4. Snapshots (A6): never tag or publish a snapshot, or add a deliberate publish path with its own dist-tag.\n5. Dist-tag policy: keep `next` only and document, or derive the tag from the pre tag.\n6. E1 consequence: releasing one identity of a dual package becomes impossible. Confirm.\n7. T06: bump the four reports to schemaVersion 2; `[[package-set]]` globs require `eco/glob`; text tables show canonical ids; `add` keeps writing native names into changesets.\n8. W4: print-only redacted tail (20 lines, 2 KiB), deny-list with shape patterns, no persisted field.\n9. Managed-CI inferred-only releases: document that changesets are the sole input and make `status --check` flag pending-without-changeset for `auto` packages (lean), or let inference open the PR (an ADR 2 revision).\n10. Provenance: add a bot-author check to the release workflow (one jq clause), or accept the residual risk.\n11. Python dev tables: document-only, or add group tracking.\n12. Floating `@v1` action tag; platform scope (Intel mac, aarch64-linux, Windows); whether to keep the under-10-minute claim or measure it hosted.\n13. Credentials and placement for T12b: a separate `workflow_dispatch` workflow with its own scratch secrets (policy-clean in a copy, not merged), or an owner-run local script.\n\n## E. Order\n\n1. Now, no decision: A1 (ownership), A7 PR1 (redactor), A8 E1, A10 (fail-not-skip), A9 Poetry caret, hygiene PRs (metadata, MSRV job, exclude, READMEs), docs refresh plus the D01 record (ADR 12, ADRs 9 and 10).\n2. After decisions 3 to 5: A2, A3, A4, A5, A6 as existing-contract repairs.\n3. T06 P1 to P5, E2 and edge granularity, W4 PR2.\n4. T12a, then T12b and T12-DX with your credentials.\n5. Stability contract and upgrade path, spec drift fixes, ADR 12 acceptance, semver gate, OIDC if decided, release 0.12.0 (#248), then 1.0.0.\n\n## Process notes\n\n- Two agents ran `cargo publish` against crates.io without credentials (the plan challenger, three attempts, and the spec reviewer, once through a real `callisto release` in a scratch fixture). All failed on \"no token\" before any upload. Nothing was published. This broke the read-only instruction I gave.\n- The harness flagged the spec reviewer's report (\"Create Public Surface\"). It contained no instructions; treat it as ordinary data.\n- All counts that come from grep are estimates. No hosted GitHub behavior, real registry, Windows or full `just ci` run was verified.\n\n## Validation pass (2026-10-20, my own runs, no agents)\n\nMethod: fresh binary from main `d1f0de357`; scratch repos under `scratchpad/validate*`, `verify_*`; a fake `cargo` and a local bare remote for release flows (infrastructure reused from an agent, read first); source greps for static claims.\n\nReproduced on the real binary by me:\n\n| Finding | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| E007 co-located Cargo + dynamic pyproject | Confirmed |\n| A1 bare-tag adoption (S3), plus S3b: after the npm rename only `npm/bar` is planned; Cargo `foo` is silently dropped | Confirmed |\n| A2 crash after publish at commit A, unrelated commit B, then `release`: tag `demo-pkg@1.0.0` lands on B | Confirmed (fake cargo; local route) |\n| A5 version already on the registry: \"already published; skipping\" then tag on HEAD | Confirmed (fake cargo). Adopting an existing exact version is ADR 3 by design; the defect is the tag target |\n| A3 pre mode on the managed route: E165, then `version` keeps bumping beta.0, beta.1, beta.2 | Confirmed |\n| A4 stale `^2.0.0-next.0` after a pre cycle (npm); Cargo compound range `>=1.2.0, <2.0.0` writes manifests and changelogs then fails with E208, rerun gives E121 | Confirmed |\n| A6 snapshot rewrites the manifest and `release --dry-run` then plans a publish and tag of `0.0.0-abc-<sha>` | Confirmed for the plan. A real `release` refuses the dirty tree (E267) unless the snapshot is committed, so severity is lower than first written |\n| A7 `Bearer npm_...` printed in cleartext (E163 text, live stderr, JSON); E176 shows a Rust Debug dump and \"the observing command failed\" with no tool text | Confirmed |\n| A8 E1: `--package npm/dual` plans only the npm publish and its tag; over-serialization: `cargo/rs` publish waits on `cargo/dual` and `npm/dual`; E2: product forge publish prerequisites are the draft and uploads only (source `derive.rs:737-738`) | Confirmed |\n| A9 Poetry `^0.1.0` not rewritten while the dependent is bumped; `>=0.1.0,<0.2` rewritten to `>=0.2.0, <1` | Confirmed |\n| A12 unknown changeset entry: file stays, `app` bumps 0.3.0 to 0.3.1 and again to 0.3.2 with no new changeset; no unknown-package diagnostic | Confirmed. The stay-on-disk part is what VER-AGG-03 specifies; the missing warning and repeat bump are the defects |\n| Spec drift: dirty worktree is E267 and shallow clone is E266 (specs say E051); E049 appears only in the spec; matrix JSON has a `command` key (MX-OUT-03 says none); `version` creates and stages `Cargo.lock` when none is tracked (VER-APPLY-14 says existing); VER-AGG-03 promises a warning | Confirmed |\n\nConfirmed by reading files:\n- Per-crate metadata: only `edition` and `repository` inherited; no `rust-version`, `keywords`, `categories`, `homepage`.\n- No `cargo-semver-checks`, MSRV job or scheduled workflow; Dependabot covers `github-actions` only; 2 fuzz targets; `AGPL-3.0-only` allowed and `wildcards = \"allow\"` in `deny.toml`; `unwrap_used` and `expect_used` set to allow; `result_large_err` allowed in 3 places; `fs2` declared and unused.\n- Docs: `how-callisto-works.md:81-83` stale; `releasing.md:24` and `:58` stale; ADRs 9 and 10 Proposed; README, SECURITY.md and `how-callisto-works.md` say pre-v1; `publishing.md:85` tells users to map `PYPI_TOKEN` to `TWINE_PASSWORD` though `run-release.sh:29-30` does; `--help` banner says \"Rust workspaces\"; E227 detail advertises `cargo:pkg`; `tag.rs:71` comment is stale.\n- Real-registry tests `return` after an `eprintln` when a tool is missing and the file is Linux-only.\n- The generated simple workflow has no `concurrency:` group; the matrix template and Callisto's own workflow do.\n- Snapshots and all prereleases publish to npm tag `next` (`derive.rs:397`).\n- The policy script allows `id-token` only for `build-artifact`.\n- Release binaries: 3 targets (aarch64-apple, x86_64 linux gnu and musl).\n\nNot independently validated (agent evidence only):","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"4a2d2041-b252-4ab7-9760-50b153c06b66","timestamp":"2026-10-21T18:17:32.501Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# v1 verification and adversarial review (2026-10-20)\n\nLocal only, never PR it. Baseline: main `d1f0de357` (v0.11.0). Twelve read-only research passes, each against the real binary, scratch repos and source. I re-ran these myself and they reproduce: E007 (Maturin), bare-tag adoption (S3), stale prerelease range after a pre cycle (S1), pre mode failing on the managed route (E165), the `Bearer` token leak in E163, `id-token` banned outside `build-artifact` by the policy script, and `edition = \"2021\"`. Everything else below is an agent finding with its evidence tag, not independently re-run. Scratch evidence is under `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c/scratchpad/r2/` (`t06`, `owner`, `graph`, `redact`, `small`, `verify`, `onedot`, `arch`, `specs`, `rust`, `pub`, `plan`).\n\nCorrection to D01-DECISIONS.md: the E101 spec and code do not disagree. Two default templates cannot collide (E100 forbids duplicate ids), so `has_default && ids.len() > 1` is equivalent to WS-ID-08. The real gap is that two packages with the same explicit `tag-template` pass silently. The stale `default_for` doc comment (`tag.rs:71`) is confirmed.\n\n## Can we tackle all of v1?\n\nD01 no longer blocks T06 or T08. The plan was incomplete, though: the review found defects that no task covers, and the work is about 25 PRs, not one push. Cargo builds and `just ci` stay serial.\n\n## A. Defects in no plan task (existing contracts, start now)\n\n| # | Defect | Evidence | Severity |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| A1 | A package renamed or lookalike adopts another package's tag; after a rename the real Cargo `foo` is treated as already tagged and never published (S3b) | Reproduced twice | High: silent skipped publish |\n| A2 | The local and generated-simple routes release HEAD, not the commit that introduced the version. A crashed run at A then `release` at B tags B with code that never shipped. Concurrent runs make a rerun fail permanently with E167 whose help is wrong. The generated simple workflow has no `concurrency:` group | Reproduced (agent) | High |\n| A3 | Pre-release mode fails on the managed route (E165 no changeset consumed), and `version` keeps bumping beta.0, beta.1, beta.2 with no changeset | Reproduced (me and agent) | High: prereleases only work locally |\n| A4 | After a pre cycle, a dependent keeps `^2.0.0-next.0`; a later major leaves it excluding the new dependency; `version` exits 0 with only a warning. Also: an unrepresentable peer or compound range is a warning, and a Cargo compound range half-applies the tree then fails at lockfile refresh (E208, then E121 on rerun) | Reproduced (me for npm) | High: wrong published ranges |\n| A5 | A foreign or already-published untagged version is adopted and tagged (\"already published; skipping\", then tags HEAD). No check that the registry package belongs to this repo | Reproduced (agent, `itoa`) | Medium-High |\n| A6 | Snapshot: rewrites every package with no changeset, leaves dependents on stable ranges, and `release --dry-run` after it plans a real git tag and npm publish. All prereleases and snapshots publish to dist-tag `next` | Reproduced (agent) | Medium-High, one-way door (dist-tag) |\n| A7 | Secret redaction is exact env value plus URL userinfo. A token not in a known variable (`Bearer npm_...`) prints in cleartext in live stderr, E163 text and the JSON error. Indeterminate observations (E176) show no tool text at all; E157 has no cause | Reproduced (me and agent) | Medium (security hygiene) |\n| A8 | Dual Cargo+npm `--package` selection plans the shared tag after one publish (E1); product announcement does not wait for a plugin's publish (E2); a dependent waits on every publish of its dependency (over-serialization) | Reproduced | Medium |\n| A9 | Poetry caret or tilde on a co-released dependency is not rewritten (only `==`, `~=`, `>=`, `>=,<` are); `>=0.1.0,<0.2` is rewritten to `>=0.2.0, <1`, widening past the 0.x boundary; Python dev tables are silently skipped | Reproduced (agent) | Medium |\n| A10 | Real-registry tests skip silently and report as passes; the PyPI test bypasses production binding and its index is HTML (production needs JSON); the file is Linux-only | Source and reproduced | Medium: false assurance |\n| A11 | A failed release cannot be inspected read-only; a publish that landed then reports E163 \"retry\" | Reproduced | Medium-Low |\n| A12 | `version` with an unknown changeset entry leaves the file, so its resolvable entries apply again on the next run | Reproduced (agent) | Medium-Low |\n| A13 | No monotonic guard: tag `libx@1.5.0` with manifest 0.1.1 plans 0.1.2 | Reproduced | Low (guard judged unsound; ownership fix covers it) |\n\n## B. Plan tasks, verified and re-sliced\n\n## C. 1.0 hygiene (Rust and publishing practice)\n\n- Metadata: crates inherit only `edition` and `repository`; add `rust-version`, `keywords`, `categories`, `homepage`; per-crate `documentation`; `exclude` tests and `proptest-regressions`; real READMEs with absolute links. (S)\n- MSRV is declared (1.96) but never tested; add a CI job. Edition 2021 -> 2024 and resolver 3; state an N-2 MSRV policy. Current stable is 1.99.1 (web). (S-M)\n- Panic hygiene: `unwrap_used` and `expect_used` are explicitly `allow` (about 66 unwrap, 48 expect in non-test code, estimates). `#![allow(clippy::result_large_err)]` crate-wide. (M)\n- `cargo-semver-checks` runs nowhere in CI; about 1,050 `pub` items across four library crates; `#[non_exhaustive]` uneven (manifests 0). #249 added a field to the public `RegistryConfig` without a Breaking note. (S-M)\n- Supply chain: weekly `cargo deny` advisories, Cargo dependabot, remove `AGPL-3.0-only` allowance, dead deps (`path-slash`, `fs2`), consider `cargo auditable`. (S)\n- Fuzz targets: 2 (`parse_changeset`, `parse_package_id`); none for the manifest editors. (M)\n- Publishing practice (2026 norm): crates.io, npm and PyPI trusted publishing (OIDC) and PyPI attestations; GitHub immutable releases; checksum sidecars (cargo-dist default). Callisto still needs `CARGO_REGISTRY_TOKEN`, `NPM_TOKEN` and `PYPI_TOKEN`; `.github/tests/verify-release-workflow-policy.sh` bans `id-token` outside `build-artifact` (my check) and its self-test requires `execute` to hold exactly the one secret. AGENTS.md does not ban OIDC in `execute`. First publish must be manual on crates.io and npm; the bootstrap is undocumented. Immutable releases make the documented `gh release delete-asset` recovery impossible after publish.\n- Docs stale at 1.0: README and SECURITY.md say pre-v1; `how-callisto-works.md` lines 81-83 still list three limits that shipped; `releasing.md` retry limit and napi roster; ADRs 9 and 10 are still Proposed although shipped; `publishing.md` says to map `PYPI_TOKEN` to `TWINE_PASSWORD` though the action does; `init`/`--help` banner says \"Rust workspaces\"; E227 help still advertises `cargo:pkg`.\n- Spec drift: about 13 of about 95 sampled criteria are false or partly true (14%). Examples: dirty worktree is E267 and shallow clone is E266, not E051; VER-CS-07 cites E049, which does not exist; VER-AGG-03 says `version` warns on an unknown package and it does not; MX-OUT-03 says matrix JSON has no `command` key and it does; VER-APPLY-14 says \"existing lockfile\" but `version` creates one; decision `edgeKind` spells `\"Runtime\"` vs `\"peer\"`. Error codes: 259 in docs and code match exactly; 154 are in no spec; 4 documented codes are never constructed (E050, E161, E248, E253); some duplicate meanings. Coverage: `compose-pr-body`, `release inspect`, `release build-python`, `previous-tag-templates`, the tag-template grammar and most action inputs have no criterion.\n- Contracts to pin before 1.0 (one-way doors): tag format (promotion flips the namespace), report key forms, config keys (`deny_unknown_fields`, no schema version), decision file path and schema, dist-tag policy, error-code stability, action inputs, which library API is public, `schemaVersion` meaning.\n- Platform coverage: release binaries are aarch64-apple, x86_64-linux gnu and musl only; no Intel mac, aarch64-linux or Windows.\n- Version strategy: a fixed group of all five crates means any library break forces a CLI major; `callisto-cli:major` plans all five from 0.11.0 to 1.0.0. #248 is the 0.12.0 release (8 changesets, no status checks).\n\n## D. Decisions needed from the owner\n\n1. OIDC: allow `id-token: write` on `execute` (secrets optional) and change the policy script, or keep long-lived tokens for 1.0 and document it.\n2. Library crates at 1.0: only `callisto-cli` at 1.0 with the libraries documented unstable and split out of the fixed group (agents' lean), or all four.\n3. Pre-release mode on the managed route (A3): support it (needs a verification rule that accepts retained changesets and no empty bump churn) or document it as local-only.\n4. Snapshots (A6): never tag or publish a snapshot, or add a deliberate publish path with its own dist-tag.\n5. Dist-tag policy: keep `next` only and document, or derive the tag from the pre tag.\n6. E1 consequence: releasing one identity of a dual package becomes impossible. Confirm.\n7. T06: bump the four reports to schemaVersion 2; `[[package-set]]` globs require `eco/glob`; text tables show canonical ids; `add` keeps writing native names into changesets.\n8. W4: print-only redacted tail (20 lines, 2 KiB), deny-list with shape patterns, no persisted field.\n9. Managed-CI inferred-only releases: document that changesets are the sole input and make `status --check` flag pending-without-changeset for `auto` packages (lean), or let inference open the PR (an ADR 2 revision).\n10. Provenance: add a bot-author check to the release workflow (one jq clause), or accept the residual risk.\n11. Python dev tables: document-only, or add group tracking.\n12. Floating `@v1` action tag; platform scope (Intel mac, aarch64-linux, Windows); whether to keep the under-10-minute claim or measure it hosted.\n13. Credentials and placement for T12b: a separate `workflow_dispatch` workflow with its own scratch secrets (policy-clean in a copy, not merged), or an owner-run local script.\n\n## E. Order\n\n1. Now, no decision: A1 (ownership), A7 PR1 (redactor), A8 E1, A10 (fail-not-skip), A9 Poetry caret, hygiene PRs (metadata, MSRV job, exclude, READMEs), docs refresh plus the D01 record (ADR 12, ADRs 9 and 10).\n2. After decisions 3 to 5: A2, A3, A4, A5, A6 as existing-contract repairs.\n3. T06 P1 to P5, E2 and edge granularity, W4 PR2.\n4. T12a, then T12b and T12-DX with your credentials.\n5. Stability contract and upgrade path, spec drift fixes, ADR 12 acceptance, semver gate, OIDC if decided, release 0.12.0 (#248), then 1.0.0.\n\n## Process notes\n\n- Two agents ran `cargo publish` against crates.io without credentials (the plan challenger, three attempts, and the spec reviewer, once through a real `callisto release` in a scratch fixture). All failed on \"no token\" before any upload. Nothing was published. This broke the read-only instruction I gave.\n- The harness flagged the spec reviewer's report (\"Create Public Surface\"). It contained no instructions; treat it as ordinary data.\n- All counts that come from grep are estimates. No hosted GitHub behavior, real registry, Windows or full `just ci` run was verified.\n\n## Validation pass (2026-10-20, my own runs, no agents)\n\nMethod: fresh binary from main `d1f0de357`; scratch repos under `scratchpad/validate*`, `verify_*`; a fake `cargo` and a local bare remote for release flows (infrastructure reused from an agent, read first); source greps for static claims.\n\nReproduced on the real binary by me:\n\n| Finding | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| E007 co-located Cargo + dynamic pyproject | Confirmed |\n| A1 bare-tag adoption (S3), plus S3b: after the npm rename only `npm/bar` is planned; Cargo `foo` is silently dropped | Confirmed |\n| A2 crash after publish at commit A, unrelated commit B, then `release`: tag `demo-pkg@1.0.0` lands on B | Confirmed (fake cargo; local route) |\n| A5 version already on the registry: \"already published; skipping\" then tag on HEAD | Confirmed (fake cargo). Adopting an existing exact version is ADR 3 by design; the defect is the tag target |\n| A3 pre mode on the managed route: E165, then `version` keeps bumping beta.0, beta.1, beta.2 | Confirmed |\n| A4 stale `^2.0.0-next.0` after a pre cycle (npm); Cargo compound range `>=1.2.0, <2.0.0` writes manifests and changelogs then fails with E208, rerun gives E121 | Confirmed |\n| A6 snapshot rewrites the manifest and `release --dry-run` then plans a publish and tag of `0.0.0-abc-<sha>` | Confirmed for the plan. A real `release` refuses the dirty tree (E267) unless the snapshot is committed, so severity is lower than first written |\n| A7 `Bearer npm_...` printed in cleartext (E163 text, live stderr, JSON); E176 shows a Rust Debug dump and \"the observing command failed\" with no tool text | Confirmed |\n| A8 E1: `--package npm/dual` plans only the npm publish and its tag; over-serialization: `cargo/rs` publish waits on `cargo/dual` and `npm/dual`; E2: product forge publish prerequisites are the draft and uploads only (source `derive.rs:737-738`) | Confirmed |\n| A9 Poetry `^0.1.0` not rewritten while the dependent is bumped; `>=0.1.0,<0.2` rewritten to `>=0.2.0, <1` | Confirmed |\n| A12 unknown changeset entry: file stays, `app` bumps 0.3.0 to 0.3.1 and again to 0.3.2 with no new changeset; no unknown-package diagnostic | Confirmed. The stay-on-disk part is what VER-AGG-03 specifies; the missing warning and repeat bump are the defects |\n| Spec drift: dirty worktree is E267 and shallow clone is E266 (specs say E051); E049 appears only in the spec; matrix JSON has a `command` key (MX-OUT-03 says none); `version` creates and stages `Cargo.lock` when none is tracked (VER-APPLY-14 says existing); VER-AGG-03 promises a warning | Confirmed |\n\nConfirmed by reading files:\n- Per-crate metadata: only `edition` and `repository` inherited; no `rust-version`, `keywords`, `categories`, `homepage`.\n- No `cargo-semver-checks`, MSRV job or scheduled workflow; Dependabot covers `github-actions` only; 2 fuzz targets; `AGPL-3.0-only` allowed and `wildcards = \"allow\"` in `deny.toml`; `unwrap_used` and `expect_used` set to allow; `result_large_err` allowed in 3 places; `fs2` declared and unused.\n- Docs: `how-callisto-works.md:81-83` stale; `releasing.md:24` and `:58` stale; ADRs 9 and 10 Proposed; README, SECURITY.md and `how-callisto-works.md` say pre-v1; `publishing.md:85` tells users to map `PYPI_TOKEN` to `TWINE_PASSWORD` though `run-release.sh:29-30` does; `--help` banner says \"Rust workspaces\"; E227 detail advertises `cargo:pkg`; `tag.rs:71` comment is stale.\n- Real-registry tests `return` after an `eprintln` when a tool is missing and the file is Linux-only.\n- The generated simple workflow has no `concurrency:` group; the matrix template and Callisto's own workflow do.\n- Snapshots and all prereleases publish to npm tag `next` (`derive.rs:397`).\n- The policy script allows `id-token` only for `build-artifact`.\n- Release binaries: 3 targets (aarch64-apple, x86_64 linux gnu and musl).\n\nNot independently validated (agent evidence only):","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"48631355-5c11-43cb-ae0e-494e8660626a","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/plans","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","branch":"stack/docs-v1","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":3,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/plans","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c4187a56-ce94-44df-93c6-e00571bd84a9","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/pl