{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","id":"6b6b6b28-3c45-46a0-b3b8-3d69d6f12643","timestamp":"2026-10-21T18:18:45.328Z","version":"2.1.304","querySource":"repl_main_thread:outputStyle:Concise","shapeHash":"ee2ce0cf87ce746ce6943833acc69476f1a369dffdb71d54a65c7c6f8ebb17d5","params":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"high"}},"base":"8c9702a4-af6f-4c18-8726-29e63a955cd4","keep":38,"tail":["8ceb440cd700931ce93d73e026723c40cc2c1433b5375a0c12011902527f5edc","26d78285b4137c31fcae3787c8b86095efa8c12a0445ee7ae2a569022a0c073f","78e7678114e9652a7222833383e21bf20bf685ebe245dab844ada6e28effa078"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",40,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"7cbd0977759d34285cfb87ed30be29b6a5fce274b14d6e8fa64193ac4b1bfbd1"}
{"parentUuid":"7e3d6b51-1e88-4bb4-99eb-aac71346caa6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFqr6AAWhQJXZr5CjcV7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written proposals for all 13 decisions in section D of the v1 review, plus the earlier defects (A2 to A6) that were waiting on them. They're saved locally in `.claude/plans/DECISION-PROPOSALS-2026-10-21.md`. These come from the review evidence and ADR 12, not from new tests against real registries.\n\n**Decide these now, because changing them after 1.0 breaks users:**\n- **Dist-tag (#5):** derive it from the pre-release identifier, so `1.0.0-beta.1` publishes to `beta`. Fall back to `next`, and never use `latest` for a prerelease. Today everything goes to `next`.\n- **T06 wire shape (#7):** yes to all four. Bump `schemaVersion` to 2 on the four reports, require `eco/glob` in package sets, show canonical ids in text tables, and keep native names in changesets.\n- **E317 (bare names in config):** go ahead. ADR 12 already says to reject new bare and colon-form aliases. The fix-it shows the exact `eco/name`, and I convert this repo's `callisto.toml` in the same PR.\n\n**Recommendations you can approve in bulk:**\n\n| # | Decision | Recommendation |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | OIDC trusted publishing | Keep tokens for 1.0 and document it. Add OIDC as an opt-in after 1.0 |\n| 2 | Crates at 1.0 | Only `callisto-cli`. Libraries stay 0.x and documented unstable, and leave the fixed group |\n| 3 | Pre mode on the managed route | Local-only for 1.0. `version` with no changeset in pre mode must not bump again, and the managed route fails early with one clear error |\n| 4 | Snapshots | Never tag or publish one. `release` refuses a snapshot version |\n| 6 | Dual packages | Already shipped in #255. Confirm and document |\n| 8 | Redaction tail | Print-only redacted tail, 20 lines or 2 KiB, no wire change |\n| 9 | Inferred-only managed releases | Changesets are the only input in managed CI. `status --check` flags a pending release without a changeset |\n| 10 | Provenance | Add the bot-author check unless it counts as an approval gate under your release policy. I'll check the policy script first |\n| 11 | Python dev tables | Document-only, with a loud warning naming the file |\n| 12 | `@v1`, platforms, 10-minute claim | Publish a floating `v1` beside immutable version tags. Add Intel mac and aarch64-linux. Windows stays unsupported until it has CI. Drop the \"under 10 minutes\" claim until it's measured |\n| 13 | Real-registry check (T12b) | An owner-run local script against scratch registries. A hosted workflow with secrets would break your release policy |\n\n**The earlier defects:**\n- **A2 (local route releases HEAD):** bind the tag and publish to the commit that introduced the version. This needs a short design spike, and I'm less sure of the exact rule.\n- **A4 (stale ranges after a pre cycle):** rewrite dependents' ranges when the dependency graduates. Unrepresentable peer or compound ranges become a hard error before any write.\n- **A5 (foreign published version):** keep adopting an exact published version (ADR 3), and warn rather than block if the registry metadata doesn't match the origin remote.\n\n**Without waiting on you:** the CI hygiene PR (MSRV, scheduled `cargo deny`, Cargo dependabot, semver-checks) and a `concurrency:` group for the generated simple workflow. I start both on your go.\n\n**Needs input:** please confirm the dist-tag rule, the `schemaVersion` 2 bump with its three companions, and E317. Then say whether to start the CI hygiene PR now.\n\nresult: Proposals and recommendations for all 13 pending decisions plus the A2 to A6 repairs are saved in `.claude/plans/DECISION-PROPOSALS-2026-10-21.md`; I need your confirmation on the dist-tag rule, the `schemaVersion` 2 bump and E317 before building them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_